    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Lambda: Capture By Value"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is similar to calling a function by value. Here, the actual value is copied when the lambda is created."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A basic lambda expression with capture by value looks as follows:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "int main() {\n\n    int num_main = 100;\n\n    // get access to num_main from the enclosing function\n    auto my_lambda = [num_main] () {\n        cout << num_main;\n    };\n\n   ... ... ...\n\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the lambda and the num_main variables have been declared inside the main() function. So, the capture clause [num_main] allows the lambda to access the num_main variable from the main() function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "More specifically, this capture clause allows the lambda to access a copy of the value of the num_main variable."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If we remove num_main from the capture clause, we will get an error since num_main cannot be accessed from the lambda body."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
